17. TWELVE MANDATORY PRODUCTION ACCEPTANCE GATES

Every major workflow must pass all twelve gates.

GATE 1 — UI EVENT

The actual interface triggers the intended operation.

GATE 2 — CLIENT HANDLER

The correct handler receives and validates the request.

GATE 3 — API ROUTE

The real backend endpoint is called.

GATE 4 — AUTHENTICATION AND RBAC

The identity and permissions are verified.

GATE 5 — TENANT ISOLATION

Unauthorized cross-tenant access is rejected.

GATE 6 — SERVICE LOGIC

The actual business logic executes.

GATE 7 — DATABASE OPERATION

The correct records are persisted.

GATE 8 — EXTERNAL PROVIDER RESPONSE

The real external service responds where required.

GATE 9 — READ-BACK VERIFICATION

The persisted or externally created resource is independently retrieved and checked.

GATE 10 — AUDIT LOG

The action and result are recorded.

GATE 11 — AUTOMATED TESTS

The workflow and relevant failure cases pass automated tests.

GATE 12 — FAILURE, RETRY AND ROLLBACK

Failures are handled safely and recovery is verified.

Required evidence chain

UI Event
→ Client Handler
→ API Route
→ Authentication/RBAC
→ Tenant Isolation
→ Service Logic
→ Database Operation
→ External Provider Response
→ Read-back Verification
→ Audit Log
→ UI Update.

Each gate must have a status:

PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED, NOT_IMPLEMENTED or NOT_APPLICABLE.

Every PASS must include evidence.

